A||||6||Cliff D.||Fuel rail won't hold pressure||||5
Z||000000||Cliff D.||11-08-1999||07:41 AM||||When I turn the key to "on", my pressure goes to 43, but when the pump shuts off, it drops to virtually zero within 5 seconds. My service manual says to turn on the pump and pinch the flex hose after the inline filter as the next step in diagnosis. What the hell kind of joke is this? How can I be under the car, at the pressure meter, and turning the ignition key all at the same time. I see no signs of leaks anywhere on the lines. Should I skip this step and test the injectors and regulator. I don't think it is the cold start valve because I can't hold pressure even after running closed loop for a few minuutes.||||reg||5
Z||000001||fieroshop||11-08-1999||11:11 AM||||The way you pinch it is by using a small pair of vise grips. That way you will be able to see everything from up on top.||||reg||6
Z||000002||fierospeeder||11-08-1999||07:31 PM||||i bought a fuel pressure tester cost a nice 34 bucks, i was wondering what my moms 2.8L celebrity pressure was.  The car wouldn't be able to hold acceleration after a hard turn.  The pressure is fine, and when the key is off, my line has a pressure of 20psi.  to test the fuel regulator pull the vacuum line off it or from the throttle body, dont know how it looks on the fiero.  The pressure should increase to 40-50, overall increase from being at idle. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cliff D.||11-08-1999||07:45 PM||||My patience paid off. I waited through my whole day off for my wife to get home so she could turn my key for 2 seconds. I did get the hose with the vice grips, and the pressure held. Now my prime suspect is the intank pump, not the injectors. Thanks guys.||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||11-09-1999||01:58 AM||||where did you pinch the line?<P>sounds like you pinched the return line if you saw pressure at the fuel rail. if you pinched the line from the fuel pump you wouldn't see preasure at the rail.<P>that being the case...... your problem would be the fuel preasure regulator.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Cliff D.||11-10-1999||12:25 AM||||I did get the right hose. That is why I needed my wife's help. I had her turn the key which sent fuel to the motor. When I heard the pump shut off, I pinched the hose and it held the fuel which she supplied. I did check the return hose and that one did not hold pressure.||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||11-10-1999||01:27 PM||||ich. yup... that's the check valve in the fuel pump alright. nasty job that.||||reg||1
